AB  - Public safety risks increasingly emerge from complex, interconnected processes spanning multiple domains, posing challenges for traditional methods in tracking their evolution. While open-source intelligence (OSINT) offers rich data for risk analysis, few studies provide a unified framework to systematically examine how these risks interact and evolve. This study presents an OSINT-based analytical framework that captures risk evolution along three dimensions: intertwining, progression, and diffusion. Leveraging a contextualized topic model alongside information-theoretic metrics, the framework quantifies the relationships and uncertainties among risk topics, enabling dynamic monitoring and delivering actionable insights to support public safety governance.
