AB  - Scene text translation (STT) must rewrite translated text into complex scenes without breaking visual style, yet font rendering or template compositing often causes color and material drift and boundary artifacts. We present a style-preserving STT system that integrates OCR, machine translation, text erasure, a tri-conditional diffusion rewrite module, and scene composition into a unified pipeline. At the core of the rewrite stage, we factorize the conditions into content, appearance, and environment, and adopt an asymmetric injection strategy: content is enforced via a structure guidance branch (SGB) while appearance and environment are fused via a 12-channel early-fusion latent input. This design enables precise glyph control while inheriting source texture cues and background statistics. We further construct a synthetic English–Chinese style transfer dataset (120,000 samples) and build synthetic and real-world English-to-Chinese STT benchmarks. Experiments in this setting show improved image quality, text accuracy, and style consistency over representative academic baselines.
