KW  - Neuro-symbolic AI
KW  - Evolutionary optimization
KW  - Modular neural networks
KW  - Memory-augmented learning
KW  - Meta-learning
AB  - Artificial intelligence has made significant strides with deep learning, yet critical challenges remain in generalization, adaptability, and interpretability. To address these limitations, we propose Neuro-Symbolic Evolutionary Networks (NSEN), a novel hybrid framework that integrates modular neural architectures, symbolic reasoning, and evolutionary optimization into a unified system. NSEN leverages modular neural components for specialized task execution, symbolic knowledge representation for structured reasoning, and evolutionary algorithms for dynamic optimization of both parameters and network structure. A memory-augmented subsystem, comprising episodic, semantic, and procedural memory, enables efficient knowledge storage and retrieval, while meta-learning mechanisms facilitate continuous self-improvement. This architecture allows NSEN to achieve better generalization, computational efficiency, and adaptability across diverse tasks. Unlike traditional deep learning models, NSEN dynamically reconfigures its structure in response to new environments, ensuring scalability and robustness. Furthermore, the integration of symbolic reasoning enhances logical consistency and decision-making transparency, addressing the "black-box" nature of conventional neural networks. We evaluate NSEN on a range of benchmarks, including image recognition, reinforcement learning, and commonsense reasoning, demonstrating state-of-the-art ability in accuracy, resource utilization, and cross-domain generalization. Experimental results highlight NSEN’s potential in real-world applications such as autonomous systems, healthcare, and scientific discovery. By combining the strengths of neural computation, symbolic AI, and evolutionary optimization, NSEN represents a transformative step toward next-generation artificial intelligence. The proposed framework not only addresses key shortcomings of current methods but also opens new direction in creative problem-solving and lifelong learning.
ER  - 
